  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Squaring gives \\((x+2)^2=4(x-2)^2,\\) or \\(3x^2-20x+12=0.\\) Both roots satisfy the original absolute-value equation, and their sum is \\(\\frac{20}{3}=6\\frac23.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Square both sides; both sides are nonnegative",
        "Use the sum of the roots of the resulting quadratic"
      ],
